# No local data on GitHub

Operational data generated while using the app locally must never be pushed to GitHub.

## Do not

- Copy `data/database.local.json` (or any runtime DB) into `data/database.json`
- Commit `database.local.json`, `database.demo.json`, `database.wipe.json`, or similar runtime files
- Sync residents, visits, reservations, correspondence, payments, audit logs, notifications, or photos from local into the repo
- “Update the seed with my current local data” unless the user **explicitly** asks to change the seed template itself

## Allowed

- Keep using and editing `data/database.local.json` locally (it is gitignored)
- Change code, UI, tests, and `data/database.test-seed.json` for automated tests
- Change `data/database.json` only when the user explicitly asks to update the **empty/demo seed template** (not a dump of their live local DB)

## If unsure

Ask the user before touching `data/database.json`. Prefer leaving local data only on the machine / Railway volume.
